# Portfolio Project — Cursor Rules
# Stack: Next.js 14 (App Router) · Tailwind CSS · Framer Motion · Node.js · Express · Supabase · Tiptap

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

This is a personal developer portfolio website with:
- A public-facing Next.js frontend (pages: home, projects, blog list, blog post, contact)
- A private /admin section for writing and managing blog posts (Tiptap editor)
- A standalone Node.js + Express backend API
- Supabase (PostgreSQL) as the database and file storage
- Tiptap for rich-text blog editing — content stored as jsonb in Supabase

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. MONOREPO FOLDER STRUCTURE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

portfolio/
├── frontend/                  # Next.js 14 app
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── (public)/
│   │   │   ├── page.tsx               # Home / hero
│   │   │   ├── projects/page.tsx
│   │   │   ├── blog/page.tsx          # Blog list
│   │   │   ├── blog/[slug]/page.tsx   # Single post
│   │   │   └── contact/page.tsx
│   │   └── admin/
│   │       ├── login/page.tsx
│   │       └── posts/
│   │           ├── page.tsx           # Manage posts
│   │           └── [id]/page.tsx      # Tiptap editor
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── ui/                        # Shared UI primitives
│   │   ├── Editor.tsx                 # Tiptap editor wrapper
│   │   └── BlogRenderer.tsx           # Renders Tiptap JSON for public pages
│   ├── lib/
│   │   ├── api.ts                     # All React Query hooks (useBlogs, useContact etc.)
│   │   ├── schemas.ts                 # Zod schemas shared across forms
│   │   └── supabaseClient.ts          # Supabase browser client (anon key only)
│   └── types/
│       └── database.types.ts          # Auto-generated Supabase types (never edit manually)
│
└── backend/                   # Express API server
    └── src/
        ├── index.ts                   # Entry — applies middleware, mounts routers
        ├── routes/
        │   ├── contact.ts             # POST /api/contact
        │   ├── blogs.ts               # GET /api/blogs, GET /api/blogs/:slug, POST, PATCH, DELETE
        │   └── upload.ts              # POST /api/upload  (multer → Supabase Storage)
        ├── middleware/
        │   ├── auth.ts                # Verifies Supabase JWT on protected routes
        │   └── rateLimiter.ts         # express-rate-limit config
        ├── lib/
        │   └── supabase.ts            # Supabase SERVICE ROLE client — never expose to frontend
        └── types/
            └── database.types.ts      # Same generated types as frontend (copy or symlink)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# frontend/.env.local
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000       # Express backend base URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon-key>       # Safe to expose — anon key only

# backend/.env
PORT=4000
SUPABASE_URL=https://<ref>.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<service-role-key>   # NEVER expose this to the frontend
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3001           # CORS whitelist

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. DATABASE SCHEMA (Supabase / PostgreSQL)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

-- contact_submissions
id            uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid()
name          text not null
email         text not null
message       text not null
status        text default 'unread'        -- unread | read | replied
created_at    timestamptz default now()

-- blog_posts
id            uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid()
title         text not null
slug          text unique not null
excerpt       text
cover_url     text                          -- Supabase Storage public CDN URL
content       jsonb not null               -- Tiptap JSON doc node
published     boolean default false
published_at  timestamptz
created_at    timestamptz default now()
updated_at    timestamptz default now()

-- tags
id            uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid()
name          text not null
slug          text unique not null

-- blog_post_tags  (join table)
blog_post_id  uuid references blog_posts(id) on delete cascade
tag_id        uuid references tags(id) on delete cascade
primary key (blog_post_id, tag_id)

-- email_queue  (reserved for future Resend integration)
id            uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid()
to_email      text not null
subject       text not null
template      text not null
payload       jsonb
status        text default 'pending'       -- pending | sent | failed
created_at    timestamptz default now()

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. API CONTRACT (Express routes)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

Public (no auth):
  GET    /api/blogs                  List published posts — supports ?page=&limit=&tag=
  GET    /api/blogs/:slug            Single post by slug
  POST   /api/contact                Submit contact form

Admin (requires Supabase JWT via Authorization: Bearer <token>):
  POST   /api/blogs                  Create new post
  PATCH  /api/blogs/:id              Update post (title, content, published etc.)
  DELETE /api/blogs/:id              Delete post
  POST   /api/upload                 Upload image → Supabase Storage → returns { url }

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. CODING CONVENTIONS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

TYPESCRIPT
- Strict mode enabled in both frontend and backend tsconfig
- Always import DB types from database.types.ts — never write inline table types
- Use type inference where obvious; add explicit return types on all exported functions
- Prefer type over interface unless extending

NAMING
- React components: PascalCase (BlogCard.tsx, ContactForm.tsx)
- Hooks: camelCase prefixed with use (useBlogs, useContactForm)
- API route files: camelCase matching the resource (blogs.ts, contact.ts)
- DB column names: snake_case (always — mirrors Supabase generated types)
- Frontend variables/functions: camelCase
- Zod schemas: PascalCase suffixed with Schema (ContactSchema, BlogPostSchema)

REACT / NEXT.JS
- Use the App Router — never use pages/ directory
- Mark components "use client" only when they use hooks or browser APIs
- Keep server components as the default — fetch data in server components where possible
- All API calls go through React Query hooks in lib/api.ts — never fetch() inline in components
- Use next/image for all images — never bare <img> tags
- Use next/link for all internal navigation — never bare <a> tags

STYLING
- Tailwind CSS only — no inline styles, no CSS modules, no styled-components
- Follow mobile-first responsive design (sm: md: lg: breakpoints)
- Dark mode via next-themes — use dark: variants in Tailwind classes
- No hardcoded hex colors — use Tailwind color tokens only

FRAMER MOTION
- Wrap page-level animations in a layout.tsx AnimatePresence
- Use variants objects for reusable animation configs — not inline objects
- Always respect prefers-reduced-motion via useReducedMotion hook

EXPRESS BACKEND
- Every route must go through zod validation before touching the DB
- Use the service role Supabase client only in backend — never in frontend
- All routes return { data, error } shaped responses
- HTTP status codes must be semantically correct (201 for creates, 400 for validation errors, 401 for auth failures, 404 for not found)
- Never log sensitive data (tokens, passwords, email content) to console

SUPABASE
- Never use the service role key in frontend code — not even in server components
- Always use generated types from database.types.ts for all query results
- Use .select() with explicit column lists — never .select('*') in production routes
- Enable RLS on all tables — write policies before shipping any route

TIPTAP
- Editor lives in components/Editor.tsx — one wrapper component, fully reusable
- Content is always stored and retrieved as a Tiptap JSON doc node (not HTML)
- Use generateHTML() from @tiptap/html for rendering on public blog pages
- Image upload calls POST /api/upload — never upload directly from the browser to Supabase
- Required extensions: StarterKit, Image, Link, Placeholder, CharacterCount

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. PATTERNS TO ALWAYS FOLLOW
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

ADDING A NEW EXPRESS ROUTE:
1. Define the Zod schema at the top of the route file
2. Add auth middleware if the route is admin-only
3. Validate request body/params with schema.safeParse()
4. Query Supabase using the typed client
5. Return { data } on success or { error } on failure
6. Export the router and mount it in index.ts

ADDING A NEW NEXT.JS PAGE:
1. Create the file under app/(public)/ or app/admin/
2. Add a React Query hook in lib/api.ts for the data fetch
3. Use the hook in the page component — no inline fetches
4. Wrap animated sections with Framer Motion variants
5. Add metadata export for SEO

ADDING A NEW SUPABASE TABLE:
1. Write the SQL in a migration file first
2. Run supabase gen types typescript to regenerate database.types.ts
3. Copy the updated types file to both frontend/types and backend/types
4. Never manually edit database.types.ts

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8. WHAT NOT TO DO — NEVER SUGGEST THESE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

- Do not use pages/ router — App Router only
- Do not use the Supabase service role key in any frontend file
- Do not use select('*') in production — always specify columns
- Do not use inline fetch() in React components — use React Query hooks
- Do not hardcode API URLs — always use NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL env var
- Do not store Tiptap content as HTML — always store as JSON
- Do not use bare <img> or <a> tags in Next.js — use next/image and next/link
- Do not write new DB column types manually — always use generated types
- Do not skip zod validation on any Express route
- Do not commit .env or .env.local files

